> Run a command over every position in a shaped region, spread across ticks.

name: Generation
slug: bookshelf-generation
version: 5.0.0
tags: runtime

$run = #[command(slash="forbidden",empty="forbidden")] string

$cuboid = arguments: {
  run: $run > command to run at each position
  size: [int] @ 3 > number of positions on each axis, in the order of the function name: a negative number goes west, down or north
  batch?: int @ 1.. > positions done each tick, 256 by default
  on_finished?: $run > command to run once every position is done
}

$rectangle = arguments: {
  run: $run > command to run at each position
  size: [int] @ 2 > number of positions on each axis, in the order of the function name: a negative number goes west, down or north
  batch?: int @ 1.. > positions done each tick, 256 by default
  on_finished?: $run > command to run once every position is done
}

$out = state > the command runs at each position, over several ticks when there are more than `batch`


feature function on_cuboid/xyz
  > Run a command at each position of a cuboid, along x, then y, then z.
  authors: Aksiome
  created: 2026/02/15 26.1
  updated: 2026/10/13 26.3

  context position > corner the cuboid starts from
  context dimension > dimension of the cuboid
  input $cuboid
  output $out


